# CS 363 - Project 2: Neo4j Graph Database Queries

A collection of Cypher queries for Neo4j demonstrating graph database operations on a university student records system.

## Overview

This project implements 18 query scripts and 5 data modification scripts using Cypher Query Language to interact with a graph database modeling:
- Students and their attributes (name, SSN, gender, addresses)
- Degrees (majors/minors at various levels)
- Courses and registrations
- Departments and their offerings

## Files

- **queries.txt** - 18 Cypher queries for data retrieval and analysis
- **ModifyRecords.txt** - 5 scripts for updating, deleting, and modifying graph data

## Query Highlights

- Basic pattern matching and filtering
- Relationship traversal (Student → Degree, Department → Course)
- Aggregations (COUNT, AVG, SUM)
- Set operations (UNION)
- Subqueries and conditional logic
- Shortest path finding
- Complex filtering with CASE expressions

## Data Modification Operations

- Property updates (SET)
- Relationship deletion
- Node and relationship cleanup with cascading deletes
- Conditional deletion based on aggregated criteria

## Prerequisites

- Neo4j Database (4.x or 5.x)
- Graph data model with Student, Course, Degree, and Department nodes
- Relationships: Majors, Minors, Registers, Offers, Administers

